   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JER.45.1#p1-473ccaa9",
     "text": "Who was Jeremiah's disciple, and wrote his prophecies under him.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "Baruch the son of Neriah"
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/JER.45.1#p2-da246e4c",
     "text": "Of which read Jer 36:9,10.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "words in a book from the",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Jer 36:9,10",
       "ref": "JER.36.9"
      },
      {
       "text": "Jer 36:9,10",
       "ref": "JER.36.10"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JER.45.3",
   "range": "JER.45.3",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "da1d4b64",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JER.45.3#p1-da1d4b64",
     "text": "Baruch moved with an inconsiderate zeal for Jeremiah's imprisonment, but chiefly for the destruction of the people and the temple makes this lamentation, as in Ps 6:6.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "fainted in my sighing",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ps 6:6",
       "ref": "PSA.6.6"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JER.45.4",
   "range": "JER.45.4",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2614173d",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JER.45.4#p1-2614173d",
     "text": "Meaning that God could destroy this people, because he had planted them.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "break down"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/JER.45.5",
   "range": "JER.45.5",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "b7605a41",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/JER.45.5#p1-17fa9bbc",
     "text": "\"Do you think to have honour and credit?\" in which he shows his infirmity.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "thou great things for thyself"
    },
    {
     "id": "geneva/JER.45.5#p2-e408191d",
     "text": "Read Jer 21:9.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "a prize in all places where",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Jer 21:9",
       "ref": "JER.21.9"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
